# Leave the client id blank to keep Patreon in demo mode.
# The exchange runs on this site at /api/patreon.
# Set the Worker secrets with:
#   npx wrangler secret put PATREON_CLIENT_ID
#   npx wrangler secret put PATREON_CLIENT_SECRET
#
# Connecting the campaign loads membership tiers.
# On the Patreon client, enable the campaigns scope
# and add this redirect: https://<your-domain>/ops
#
# Operations panel (/ops). Worker settings, not Vite variables.
# Locally, put them in .dev.vars. In production, use `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
#   DEMO               Set to 0 to remove demo behavior: the stand-in patron,
#                      the operations password, placeholder catalogs, and the
#                      seeded demonstration rows. Leave unset to keep the demo.
#   OPS_ADMIN_EMAILS   Comma-separated emails treated as admins (bootstrap).
#   LINEAR_API_KEY     Linear personal API key. Accepted requests are filed to Linear.
#   LINEAR_TEAM_ID     Fallback Linear team UUID for queues with no team set in /ops.
#   LINEAR_LABEL_ID    Fallback Linear label UUID for queues with no label set in /ops.
#   EMAIL_FROM         Sender for commission emails (receipt, accepted, declined),
#                      on a domain onboarded to Cloudflare Email Sending.
#   EMAIL_REPLY_TO     Optional address that client replies go to.
VITE_PATREON_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_PATREON_EXCHANGE_URL=/api/patreon
VITE_PATREON_PAGE_URL=https://www.patreon.com/
